  "section_notes": "The S2 rule keeps the 5% per-model threshold but has no sales stop, and the transition is open-ended (coded as 999), so the Hearth 10 is protected from a ban. S5 sets a numeric 8/100k trigger but makes recall discretionary with open-ended corrective action, which shields the Ember 8 at 9.9/100k. Buyers do receive numeric per-model failure rates, while the general public does not."
